1
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:16,900
人把记忆留在岩壁，又把思想写进文字。
We left memory on stone, and thought in writing.

2
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:20,300
图灵问：机器能思考吗？
Turing asks: Can machines think?

3
00:00:20,550 --> 00:00:23,900
几十年后，GPT 从这场探索中长出。
Decades later, GPT grows from this wider pursuit.

4
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:29,000
Transformer，让词语在语境中彼此关联。
The Transformer connects words through context.

5
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:33,900
GPT 的故事，从这里长出新的枝条。
From this foundation, a new branch begins to grow.

6
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:38,800
初代 GPT，先从大量文字中学习。
The original GPT first learns from a large body of text.

7
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:43,900
预测下一个词元，再适配不同任务。
Predict the next token, then adapt to different tasks.

8
00:00:44,450 --> 00:00:49,900
到 GPT-2，文字开始连成更长的篇章。
With GPT-2, text grows into longer passages.

9
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:55,100
规模扩大，能力开始超出续写本身。
With greater scale, capabilities extend beyond continuation.

10
00:00:55,350 --> 00:01:01,900
给出几个示例，就能提示它完成新的任务。
A few examples can guide it toward a new task.

11
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:07,900
人类的示范与反馈，让回答更有用。
Human demonstrations and feedback make answers more useful.

12
00:01:08,650 --> 00:01:13,650
ChatGPT，把这些能力带进普通人的对话。
ChatGPT brings these capabilities into everyday conversation.

13
00:01:13,900 --> 00:01:19,900
一句提问，开始成为新的操作入口。
A question becomes another way into the computer.

14
00:01:20,700 --> 00:01:25,000
这个家族，开始连接文字之外的世界。
The family reaches beyond the written word.

15
00:01:25,250 --> 00:01:29,900
图像、声音，与语言汇入同一场对话。
Images, sound, and language enter the same conversation.

16
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:38,900
不只更快回答，也学习在作答前多推敲。
Beyond faster answers, more computation before responding.

17
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:44,600
看图、听声音，也能写代码、使用工具。
See, listen, write code, and use tools.

18
00:01:44,850 --> 00:01:50,900
Codex，是这个家族伸向编程的一根枝条。
Codex is one branch of the family reaching into code.

19
00:01:51,550 --> 00:01:58,900
语言，开始把一个想法变成可运行的东西。
Language begins to turn an idea into something that runs.

20
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:04,200
一代代变化，改变的不只是模型。
Across generations, more than the models has changed.

21
00:02:04,450 --> 00:02:09,900
还有我们把想法交给计算机的方式。
So has the way we bring our ideas to computers.

22
00:02:10,500 --> 00:02:13,850
过去，我们学习机器的语言。
We learned the languages of machines.

23
00:02:14,050 --> 00:02:17,900
后来，机器开始学习我们的表达。
Then machines began learning ours.

24
00:02:18,650 --> 00:02:26,800
这段家族史的下一页，从你的问题开始。
The next page of this history begins with your question.
